Z||000008||AusFiero||07-17-2001||02:10 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Huck:<BR><B>Yeah, I had some fee's... of course!!  I had to give the post office $56.32 before they would give me my parcel.<P>Duty: 6%       14.06<BR>GST:  7%       17.39<BR>PST:  8%       19.87<BR>Handleing Fee:  5.00<BR>               ------<BR>              $56.32<P>Grand total of the enclosure in Canadian dollars:  $290.65<P>Gotta love Taxes... and the customs was based on 234.33 (150 american) at 6%..<P>Huck</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm sounds like the Canadian postal service likes to rip you a little. I pay lots at this end for shipping and handling to the door at the other end then they charge you a handling fee that I have technically already paid.<BR>What is PST?<P>GST is cheaper than ours.<P>And import duties into Australia run at 25 to 52%. God I wish ours was that low. <P>Bearing that in mind though Huck I will try to work out a way to make it cheaper in future for any Canadian buyer. I also have another shipping option that can save more money but would take 3 weeks for arrival.<P>I feel bad that they hit you up for so much at the Canadian end. Did I send a Aussie Unique Cars mag with yours? Can't remember.<P>Grinthock, when you read this if yours still isn't there email me and I will chase it up. If lost I will dispatch another to you and claim the insurance at my end to save you waiting. Will still need a week or so before I am fit enough to make another though.<P>I noticed on the American customs site that anything under $1000 going into the USA usually attracts no duty or if unlucky to get hit with it is about 2.37%. Sounds like the Canadian government is as money hungry as the Aussie one.<P>Also knowing what Huck got hit up with now I will provide any Canadaian buyer who has already purchased a console a good discount on any other product they may purchase off me in future. Yes it cuts into what I make but I aim to please in a community like this and losing a few bucks my end is the least I can do. I just want everyone to be happy with what they get. <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000009||grinthock||07-17-2001||07:25 AM||||Yep JUST GOT IT  Aus, I do'nt have it YET I have to go pick it up, but I got a notice...<P>Duty: 6% 14.06<BR>GST: 7% 17.39<BR>PST: 8% 19.87<BR>Handleing Fee: 5.00<BR>------<BR>$56.32<P>That's what I have to pay too!<P>AUS Don't LOSE money on our acct, BUT a nice thing to do would be to put a note on the web site ... Canadian customs will be levied a $56 charge in $CDN by the local govt for import duty and taxes<P>Just helps us KNOW what's gonna happen<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||AusFiero||07-17-2001||08:38 PM||||Damn good idea Grinthock. I will do that on the front page of the site mentioning percentages Canadians will get charged at their end for things being delivered. Just wish I knew it earlier.<P>I also did some figures on my costs and figure I will give any future Canadian customer US$10 off the consoles. Not much I know but it will help write off a little of the extra charges and I can't really afford to go any lower. <P>USA customers please don't gripe about Canadians getting a discount but I feel their pain. We have huge taxes and duties in Australia and our dollars, like the Canadian just don't stand up against the USA dollar real well.||||reg||14
